<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Tonga Telecom, NEC in A$4 mln telecoms deal.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Tonga Telecom, NEC in A$4 mln telecoms deal.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tonga Telecom and NEC Australia, a unit of Japan's NEC Corp, said on Thursday they had signed a A$4 million deal to provided a domestic satelite system to link Tonga's five major island groups.</p>
<p>The system, consisting of five Intelsat F-3 Standard earth stations, is to be completed by December 1997 and is one of the largest ever ordered by Tonga Telecom.</p>
<p>The deal contains a technology transfer element with Tonga Telecom engineers and technical officers to be trained in Tonga and Australia to operate and maintain the system.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
